<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Polish Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1733–1735</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Polish Succession was fought from 1733 to 1735 over the succession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustus-ii-the-strong">Augustus II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustus-iii">Augustus III</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski">Stanisław Leszczyński</a>, supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>; Augustus won the Polish throne, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vienna-1738">Treaty of Vienna (1738)</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> to Stanisław for life and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> to the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> Don Carlos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Polish Succession" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LocalF15 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_of_the_Polish_Succession_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
